================================================================================
ANSIBLE MULTI-OS AWS INFRASTRUCTURE AUTOMATION REPORT
================================================================================

PROJECT OVERVIEW
----------------
The objective of this project was to automate the lifecycle of a hybrid cloud 
infrastructure environment using Ansible Core running within Windows Subsystem 
for Linux (WSL). The infrastructure encompasses multi-distribution AWS EC2 
instances provisioned via secure, vault-encrypted credentials, automated 
key-pair integrations, and OS-specific runtime conditionals.

================================================================================
TASK 1: PROVISIONING HYBRID EC2 INFRASTRUCTURE VIA ANSIBLE LOOPS
================================================================================
Objective:
Deploy three distinct EC2 instances to AWS using an Ansible looping mechanism, 
delegating the execution locally to the control node.
- Instance 1 & 2: Ubuntu LTS Server
- Instance 3: Amazon Linux / CentOS Variant
- Target Region: us-east-1 (N. Virginia)

Troubleshooting & Resolutions:
1. Error: ansible-vault: error: unrecognized arguments: -ault-password-file
   - Cause: Typo. Passed a single dash (-) instead of a double dash (--).
   - Fix: Corrected command syntax flags to use full double dashes: 
     --vault-password-file.

2. Error: [Errno 8] Exec format error ... vault.pass
   - Cause: WSL Filesystem Mount Driver Limitation. Creating the flat file 
     inside the Windows mount directory (/mnt/c/...) automatically flagged the 
     file with executable permissions. Ansible mistook it for an executable 
     script rather than a flat file. 
   - Fix: Relocated vault.pass to the native, isolated Linux home directory 
     structure (~/vault.pass) where native POSIX permissions persist perfectly. 
     Executed 'chmod 600 ~/vault.pass' to restrict access.

3. Error: InvalidAMIID.NotFound
   - Cause: Region-mismatched or outdated image tokens. 
   - Fix: Identified explicit active image IDs for us-east-1. Updated loop 
     sequence parameters to map 'ami-0e2c8caa4b6378d8c' for Ubuntu instances.

4. Error: InvalidKeyPair.NotFound
   - Cause: Passed an identity string (key_name: "ansible") that did not exist 
     in the targeted region.
   - Fix: Generated an RSA keypair named explicitly 'ansible' inside the AWS 
     us-east-1 EC2 Console and downloaded the .pem artifact.

Final Blueprint (ec2_create.yaml):
----------------------------------
---
- name: Infrastructure Lifecycle - Provision Target Lab Nodes
  hosts: localhost
  connection: local
  gather_facts: false

  tasks:
    - name: Spin Up Target Cluster Instances
      amazon.aws.ec2_instance:
        name: "{{ item.name }}"
        key_name: "ansible"
        instance_type: t3.micro
        security_group: default
        region: us-east-1
        aws_access_key: "{{ ec2_access_key }}"
        aws_secret_key: "{{ ec2_secret_key }}"
        network_interfaces:
          - assign_public_ip: true
        image_id: "{{ item.image }}" 
      loop:
        - { image: "ami-0e2c8caa4b6378d8c", name: "manage-node-1" }
        - { image: "ami-0e2c8caa4b6378d8c", name: "manage-node-2" }
        - { image: "ami-098c93bd9d114abc7", name: "manage-node-3" }


================================================================================
TASK 2: AUTOMATED PASSWORDLESS KEY CLIENT AUTHENTICATION
================================================================================
Objective:
Establish a secure connection pipeline between the local WSL shell workspace 
and the cloud nodes without interactive login prompts or parameter injection.

Troubleshooting & Resolutions:
1. Issue: ssh-copy-id connection hang/timeout
   - Cause: AWS cloud images disable password authentication by default. 
     ssh-copy-id requires initial password authentication to push a key.
   - Fix: Abandoned ssh-copy-id. Because AWS handles the ingestion of public keys 
     into cloud targets natively via key_name declarations at launch, the 
     infrastructure is natively passwordless from inception.

2. Issue: Connection Hang using ec2-user
   - Cause: Passed a mismatched administrative account identifier for an Ubuntu 
     platform node (ec2-user@44.193.81.163).
   - Fix: Adjusted variables to match OS standards: 'ubuntu' for Ubuntu systems 
     and 'ec2-user' for Amazon Linux/CentOS systems.

3. Issue: Permission denied (publickey)
   - Cause: Executed native ssh commands without providing the underlying path (-i).
   - Fix: Cached identity token using the Linux agent subsystem:
     eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
     ssh-add /home/satbat/.ssh/ansible.pem

4. Issue: Host Key Verification Prompt
   - Cause: First-time handshake security validation warning native to SSH.
   - Fix: Appended inline option -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no to bypass once, 
     and updated global ansible.cfg to ignore verification permanently: 
     host_key_checking = False.

