================================================================================
TASK 3: TARGETED GROUP TERMINATION VIA FACT-GATHERING CONDITIONALS
================================================================================
Objective:
Execute a selective playbook routine that triggers a system halt command 
(shutdown) exclusively on nodes belonging to the Debian (Ubuntu) ecosystem 
while ignoring CentOS/RedHat elements.

Troubleshooting & Resolutions:
1. Error: Unrecognized property: became
   - Cause: Syntax error. Misspelled privilege escalation directive as 'became'.
   - Fix: Standardised syntax back to its proper parameter name: 'become: true'.

2. Error: Conditional logic tracking failure
   - Cause: Mismatched syntax structure lookup or string typos ('os.family', 
     'Dedian', 'Redhat').
   - Fix: Corrected syntax to ansible_facts['os_family'] and set proper noun 
     capitalisation ('Debian' for Ubuntu; 'RedHat' for enterprise Linux).

3. Error: UNREACHABLE! Connection timed out
   - Cause: Target AWS instances were stopped or restarted, causing dynamic public 
     IP updates on the cloud control plane.
   - Fix: Polled AWS EC2 dashboard, fetched fresh active network endpoints, 
     and synchronized the connection strings within inventory.ini.

Final Blueprint (ec2_stop.yaml):
--------------------------------
---
- name: Automated Infrastructure Management - Selective Shut Down
  hosts: all
  become: true
  gather_facts: true

  tasks: 
    - name: Halt Ubuntu Target Clusters Gracefully
      ansible.builtin.command: /sbin/shutdown -h now
      when: ansible_facts['os_family'] == 'Debian'
